(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[" Sections 3.1 & 3.2", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"bf403d1f-0edc-4edc-ac82-f13259fedced"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["  Stability of Dynamic Models",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"7cbc011d-3817-428c-91ec-\
745ea2e6c44a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"Remove", "[", "\"\<Global`*\>\"", " ", "]"}], " "}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398346080413*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1119]:=",ExpressionUUID->"aca0c77a-9143-42be-85d7-8eaede366202"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Section 3.1:  Intuitive Background", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1642d155-bc45-4048-8814-26a5005c74ad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The previous chapter covered the behavior for ODE systems which are linear, \
homogeneous and autonomous.  Although the behavior of such systems is \
extremely limited, it represents a good starting point for the study of \
nonlinear systems.  Specifically, if a nonlinear system is reasonably well \
behaved, then for a sufficiently small region in the domain, the nonlinear \
system will be approximately linear.  Therefore, a basic understanding of the \
behavior of linear systems is very helpful in understanding the local \
behavior of nonlinear systems.\nPlease note that we will not study the \
behavior of nullclines because we can obtain the full vector field with a \
single ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " command."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e4cf2598-6e84-4d7d-96e0-cfa4b189dc4c"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Section 3.2:  Linearization (single first-order equation)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"076a7ab0-7ca3-466b-819a-e88f64f7c4b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Consider the following autonomous first-order nonlinear ODE:\n\t\tx ' = \
f[x]\nFor example:  \n\t\tx ' = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "4"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{"4", " ", "x"}], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "3"]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "22eaa874-6107-48c2-b49c-99b075d783d5"],
 "\nWe might first attempt to locate any equilibrium points for this \
equation.  As before, equilibrium points correspond to a zero value for x '."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398346099881*^9, 3.398346101639*^9}, {
  3.3983479034969997`*^9, 
  3.398347916337*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"85985812-446b-4ffc-85e9-716b56f1f2b3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"Solve", " ", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"0", "==", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "4"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "x"}], "-", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "+", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "3"]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "x"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398347922448*^9, 3.398347930021*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1120]:=",ExpressionUUID->"568c1309-2654-4a93-80df-281e260aacb8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The above equation indicates that this specific nonlinear ODE has exactly \
one real equilibrium point located at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4bab8f62-3208-4d0c-803f-b23da68a1078"],
 " = 1 ( i.e.  f[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "17f8c818-0089-4b9b-ac20-e8c283719c81"],
 " ] = 0 ).  Therefore, we might want to make a linear approximation to this \
ODE at the equilibrium point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d1ded5ec-a0e6-44d2-b731-f80cf11ed40e"],
 " = 1.  This can be accomplished in the usual way by expanding f[x] in a \
Taylor polynomial of degree one about the point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7e5186b5-2b3f-414a-842d-45640ed7bf89"],
 ".  Start by defining a new variable \"u\" as\n\t\tu = x - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e22c35a3-83e8-460c-9bdc-4b5b9d1884fc"],
 "\nthen\n\t\tu ' = (u + ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "94b0400f-e2d8-4e76-acb1-9c3f0136a138"],
 ")' = x ' = f[x] = f[ u + ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "73362d92-3e68-4687-a671-70a7eed44728"],
 " ] = f[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "795ebed6-49c8-4c62-ae55-5e8e45f20939"],
 " ] + f '[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "04439639-12fd-4594-95fb-6b69d871a4e7"],
 " ](x - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "67343cdb-a28f-49e4-840a-13ba1c8fdb25"],
 ") + g[ x - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8adfe00f-1a6e-4136-8380-4f33c4d7c999"],
 " ]\n\t\t                                                         = f[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3e249e0f-202c-4103-8c80-669e4985dafb"],
 " ] + f '[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fbf8d239-0a88-482f-a48e-385d4c639a62"],
 " ] u + g[ u ]\n\t\t                                                         \
=             f '[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ebd33e30-4e7f-4a75-9aed-8f603f80e580"],
 " ] u + g[ u ]\nbecause f[ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b9de5711-25c7-4637-9dd2-96a45c23513c"],
 " ] = 0.\n\nDefine f[x]:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398346103288*^9, 3.398346108717*^9}, {3.398347962234*^9,
   3.398347978737*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"eb754ed1-9b61-497d-8c75-30410c2c8036"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f", "[", "x_", "]"}], ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", "4"}], "+", 
   RowBox[{"4", " ", "x"}], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox["x", "3"]}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1121]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a5a6d95e-7719-4f13-b951-99e5ca4e803e"],

Cell["Therefore, the ODE becomes:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.39834611563*^9},ExpressionUUID->"65ba03bb-2648-4560-aacb-36ed2bb42e5a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"u", "'"}], " ", "==", "  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", " ", "'"}], "[", " ", 
     FormBox[
      SubscriptBox["x", "0"],
      TraditionalForm], " ", "]"}], " ", "u"}], " ", "+", " ", 
   RowBox[{"g", "[", " ", "u", " ", "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1122]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ba7dbbbe-a87e-4387-8609-7224bf4335df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The linear part of this ODE is:   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"4", "-", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", 
      SubscriptBox["x", "0"]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{"3", " ", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["x", "0", "2"]}]}], ")"}], "u", " "}]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"f0c0a080-f0c7-4b49-8fca-1d32d21a6845"],
 " =  a u, where \"a\" is constant.\nThe non-linear part of this ODE is:   \
g[u], which approaches zero as u \[Rule] 0.\nThe value of \"a\" determines \
the stability at the equilibrium point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     SubscriptBox["x", "0"],
     TraditionalForm], " ", "=", " ", "1"}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "25066305-896f-4b74-858a-5fad13fc3c95"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398346117323*^9, 
  3.3983461187*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"61387a43-fad7-4e1d-ad84-060481f01563"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     SubscriptBox["x", "0"],
     TraditionalForm], " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ";"}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1123]:=",ExpressionUUID->"dc3f6aca-20f1-4e84-b4cb-6878995bb42e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"4", "-", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", 
     SubscriptBox["x", "0"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{"3", " ", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["x", "0", "2"]}]}], ")"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1124]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1b33232b-62e8-4843-82e8-3d18c29d11d6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Specifically,  u ' \[TildeTilde] 5 u   ( for small values of u)\nBecause a \
= 5 > 0, then this specific equilibrium point is unstable because the linear \
ODE  u ' = 5 u   is unstable.\nThis can be readily seen by examining a \
solution in the vicinity of the equilibrium point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     SubscriptBox["x", "0"],
     TraditionalForm], " ", "=", " ", "1"}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "93b9f06a-d28f-4649-aa6a-77420b83db3c"],
 ".\nSpecifically, solve the original nonlinear ODE starting close to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     SubscriptBox["x", "0"],
     TraditionalForm], " ", "=", " ", "1"}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cce8d8c7-41c1-4176-a462-e4bf54de8025"],
 " (i.e. x[0]=1.1)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d57f94ca-a25d-46e6-b325-15b2dc644e92"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"solutionRule", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "4"}], "+", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", 
         RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "-", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], "2"], "+", 
        SuperscriptBox[
         RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], "3"]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "1.1"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", ".5"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398346439072*^9, 3.398346440935*^9}, {
  3.3983480328380003`*^9, 3.398348036793*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1125]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ceb9432c-9cbf-4947-a067-ef849f76b2d4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", " ", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", "solutionRule"}], ",", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", "\[Rule]", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", " ", "5"}], ",", "5"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"Thickness", "[", ".01", "]"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398348045574*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1126]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2cb4a5d5-19e6-4aa4-aef1-054be4e2835d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Observe that the above solution moves away from the equilibrium point.  \
Therefore, this equilibrium point is unstable.\nHowever, if a < 0 in the \
linear ODE, then the equilibrium point for the nonlinear ODE will be locally \
stable (i.e. an attractor).\n\n",
 StyleBox["Theorem 3.1",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "   A sufficient condition for an isolated equilibrium to be an attractor \
(i.e. stable) is that u = 0 is a global attractor for the linearized equation \
(i.e. a < 0)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aeb8aa0e-fc59-40e8-8f57-3bac3989d891"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Section 3.2:  Linearization (two first-order equations)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c0bdae26-eb4e-42c7-9499-8c815cf19381"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Consider the general form of a system of two ordinary differential \
equations where the field is independent of time (i.e. autonomous).\n\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\t\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x1", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\t\t", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x2", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"5b63c654-8c87-4547-8015-2bbd296d44a6"],
 "\n\nThe functions f1 and f2 are assumed to be smooth and differentiable.  \
As such, we can approximate both functions with a Taylor polynomial expanded \
about a point (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9d694335-59b9-4f69-8768-575f97f7db0e"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"c05cbdec-0e62-476e-bd20-e0da3e749695"],
 "):\n  \n  f1[x1,x2] = f1[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "28db87f6-6448-402e-b37f-e63a00afdca8"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"c34ebcd6-1b3b-4c7a-bfa1-c314145c872c"],
 "]  +  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], "  ", "f1"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"345f8df1-1116-41a1-9cba-eec9e37c6cc4"],
 "[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "40b31ba9-3702-4785-8c06-6fadb7b6017f"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"07505660-f8ea-4661-b856-5d25157f25a2"],
 "] *(x1 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f55d576b-f825-432e-866c-6468523cf4ef"],
 ")  +  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], "  ", "f1"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"3159088b-57af-4b49-a41c-d90b82a4d92f"],
 "[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a167fa6e-0804-4d22-9831-e520a880f09f"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"91fd94a3-43cb-4f72-b856-4fcc93d8d1f3"],
 "] *(x2 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"5527cf3b-7aa7-466c-98bd-e9333cac8768"],
 ")  +  g1[x1 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "063d7ea4-e0a5-40a3-aa27-e655de1799b7"],
 ",x2 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"485e330c-7a48-42f1-9ee6-ee3465c19398"],
 "]\n  \n  f2[x1,x2] = f2[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1df524a0-08a9-4807-bc83-2d4a64cb5cb2"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"bfc4514d-0ac6-4d0e-9024-3b9f825549a8"],
 "]  +  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], "  ", "f2"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"5927ceb7-20c2-4a0e-b8b7-e5227b8b975a"],
 "[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f87c966d-fb0f-481d-aec6-8a57a4d73d7d"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"00483881-cdd0-44d5-9f4d-589492dbef7d"],
 "] *(x1 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3375d72e-1952-4cd1-887f-5061cd389181"],
 ")  +  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], "  ", "f2"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"a40efefa-ea3d-4c49-9490-6eafc05c7f34"],
 "[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6a55fa1b-af4f-4743-9046-92571d614d5d"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"3d5d381e-52ab-4e1e-9a0a-73955f718731"],
 "] *(x2 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"0e227402-1a1a-40f2-a7fe-67a3718deccd"],
 ")  +  g2[x1 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0b5c3b93-00ad-4fbb-9869-9b76e89d1c20"],
 ",x2 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"f0b5d30a-94ae-45aa-ab67-8db5201c2b25"],
 "]\n    \nThe functions g1 and g2 represent the higher order terms.\nIf we \
choose the point (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7516f0f1-6618-4cca-8ba2-29f5525e4128"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"4930df98-0798-466d-9b51-156fb708bda3"],
 ") to be an equilibrium state then our Taylor polynomial approximations \
reduce to:\n     \n      f1[x1,x2] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], "  ", "f1"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"af728ae7-9d7a-4aaf-b0ac-0ac2f5f255e1"],
 "[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1ca0e5df-baeb-4a61-969b-8b6d526a641d"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"bb85c7c6-11b5-4715-9a02-367c7d1854fb"],
 "] *(x1 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "56f3c74b-3cdc-4724-80f2-e4b63c25add6"],
 ") + ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], "  ", "f1"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"d858af80-91e1-46a5-83c1-e016ecb37982"],
 "[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ae2b3eb6-0740-46e9-ba8c-871df46c758f"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"f7588dae-e25c-4584-8fc1-4864bb1e9f08"],
 "] *(x2 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"6cf80ba8-de36-4c08-948d-ded88912a307"],
 ") + g1[x1 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "eab6c8da-a727-4cf1-aa16-555cad890f79"],
 ",x2 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"9346d6c6-4a18-4efc-a6f5-f0f3a218818e"],
 "]\n      \n      f2[x1,x2] = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], "  ", "f2"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"1478c502-0d89-43f0-a505-48330b7c252a"],
 "[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a332b119-77e7-47bd-b2d3-ce6d887722db"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"1d1084f3-416a-46c5-931b-d9fc93b6133c"],
 "] *(x1 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5e692ee9-2e0f-4c89-bebf-e21f2495283d"],
 ") + ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], "  ", "f2"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"e6f58f86-138b-402d-bb75-9011294ff991"],
 "[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5a6a16fe-8adf-42ab-a989-0f45811277dd"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"47cbeb37-9ced-465b-bc78-d16e391e1f6d"],
 "] *(x2 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"affd5506-38c3-447a-b717-38c833a700d2"],
 ") + g2[x1 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "094538bf-dac3-4cf1-a642-d1d17de69f56"],
 ",x2 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"d0768d00-f611-4c89-a73b-dcbf8fdf8b8c"],
 "]\n       \nbecause:  f1[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4338fc0c-7831-43d5-b3bb-78c3a1a46aad"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"c7c3a28b-3cad-4fd0-bcfe-f87040afb9d5"],
 "] = 0 and f2[",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "714a760a-769f-434a-8b49-41d0ce60ae8e"],
 ",",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"f4b54ff9-a147-4e74-8a63-8aa94f68f3b4"],
 "] = 0 at the equilibrium point.\nIn matrix form:\n        \n         ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{"x1", "'"}]},
       {
        RowBox[{"x2", "'"}]}
      }], ")"}],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "73daa167-059e-453f-8d67-17067bda0c34"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    StyleBox[GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], "  ", 
         RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox[
            SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
            FontWeight->"Bold"], ",", 
           StyleBox[
            SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
            FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "]"}]}], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], "  ", 
         RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox[
            SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
            FontWeight->"Bold"], ",", 
           StyleBox[
            SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
            FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "]"}]}]},
       {
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], "  ", 
         RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox[
            SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
            FontWeight->"Bold"], ",", 
           StyleBox[
            SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
            FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "]"}]}], 
        RowBox[{" ", 
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], "  ", 
          RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            StyleBox[
             SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
             FontWeight->"Bold"], ",", 
            StyleBox[
             SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
             FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "]"}]}]}]}
      }],
     FontWeight->"Bold"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b4e2f353-8d00-41fe-8cb0-9b0998b146a3"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    StyleBox[GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{"x1", " ", "-", " ", 
         StyleBox[
          SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
          FontWeight->"Bold"]}]},
       {
        RowBox[{"x2", " ", "-", " ", 
         SubscriptBox["X2", "0"]}]}
      }],
     FontWeight->"Bold"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "585e105d-dabc-4a55-8721-45f45881faaf"],
 " \n         \n         \t\t+ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", " ", 
    StyleBox[GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{"g1", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"x1", " ", "-", " ", 
           StyleBox[
            SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
            FontWeight->"Bold"]}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"x2", " ", "-", " ", 
           StyleBox[
            SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
            FontWeight->"Bold"]}]}], 
         StyleBox["]",
          FontWeight->"Bold"]}]},
       {
        RowBox[{"g2", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"x1", " ", "-", " ", 
           StyleBox[
            SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
            FontWeight->"Bold"]}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"x2", " ", "-", " ", 
           StyleBox[
            SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
            FontWeight->"Bold"]}]}], "]"}]}
      }],
     FontWeight->"Bold"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontWeight->"Bold"]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a8a13c0a-5ac6-40e2-bce6-32c967d26566"],
 "        \n        \nThe matrix is the Jacobian matrix of the field \
evaluated at the equilibrium point.\n         \n        A =  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], "  ", 
        RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"], ",", 
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "]"}]}], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], "  ", 
        RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"], ",", 
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "]"}]}]},
      {
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], "  ", 
        RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"], ",", 
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "]"}]}], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], "  ", 
        RowBox[{"f2", " ", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"], ",", 
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "]"}]}]}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"f964591e-825e-4c3f-a800-6d599db6db2f"],
 "\n         \nAs expressed above, the equation is expanded about an \
equilibrium point which is usually not the origin.  For convenience, it is \
desirable to change our variables to move the point of interest to the \
origin.\n          \n\t          u1 = x1 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "057daceb-05e8-4b66-8528-04e4b1610c07"],
 "\n\t          u2 = x2 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fbdbbb9f-2e62-4f0b-b0ca-1dad0c66824c"],
 "\n          \nMaking the indicated change in the above equation yields:\n",
 StyleBox["            \n              ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{"u1", "'"}]},
      {
       RowBox[{"u2", "'"}]}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"163fed28-f418-41ca-b81a-633ab17ac457"],
 StyleBox[" = ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], "  ", 
        RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"], ",", 
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "]"}]}], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], "  ", 
        RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"], ",", 
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "]"}]}]},
      {
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], "  ", 
        RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"], ",", 
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "]"}]}], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], "  ", 
        RowBox[{"f2", " ", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"], ",", 
          StyleBox[
           SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "]"}]}]}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"5ace572a-1997-493d-9bc6-1afd7d579867"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {"u1"},
      {"u2"}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"75844132-1dc2-4e0a-8f61-7f98600498e3"],
 StyleBox[" \n              \n              \t\t",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "+",
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{"g1", "[", 
        RowBox[{"u1", ",", "u2"}], "]"}]},
      {
       RowBox[{"g2", "[", 
        RowBox[{"u1", ",", "u2"}], "]"}]}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"fdfefd4d-19f5-401f-8306-7098bcd45811"],
 "\n              \nIn the new variables, the equilibrium point will be \
relocated to the origin.  The form of the new equation is:\n                \n\
               ",
 StyleBox[" U' = A*U + G[U]",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n                \nWe now see that the nonlinear ODE has a linear part:    \
   \n                 \n                ",
 StyleBox[" U' \[TildeTilde] A*U",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n                 \nand a nonlinear part ",
 StyleBox["G[U]",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " which represents the difference between the linear and the nonlinear \
equations and approaches 0 in the vicinity of the equilibrium point (i.e.  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["1", 
       RowBox[{"||", "U", "||"}]], 
      RowBox[{"G", "[", "U", "]"}]}], " ", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
        {"0"},
        {"0"}
       }], ")"}]}],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "57692a76-b7f4-48c2-a38c-7be34d309c51"],
 " as ||U|| \[Rule] 0).  \nThe linear equation (which will also use the \
variable U, i.e. U' = F[U] and U' = A U) allows us to study the local \
stability of the nonlinear equation.  For our purposes, we will assume that \
the nonlinear equation can be approximated with sufficient accuracy by the \
linear equation so that the stability of the nonlinear equation can be \
understood by studying the behavior of the linear equation.  One should \
understand that the linear approximation is only valid locally, and not \
globally.  Thus our stability analysis will be valid only for orbits \
sufficiently close to the equilibrium point under analysis  (i.e. local \
stability).  In general, if the linear system is globally asymptotically \
stable, then we expect the nonlinear system to be locally asymptotically \
stable.  However, we will give examples later that illustrate that for the \
cases of neutral stability and instability, that the behavior of the \
nonlinear system can not be accurately predicted from the behavior of the \
corresponding linear system.\n\n",
 StyleBox["Theorem 3.2",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 StyleBox["  ",
  FontSize->14],
 "Let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {
       StyleBox[
        SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
        FontWeight->"Bold"]},
      {
       StyleBox[
        SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
        FontWeight->"Bold"]}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "53d4d929-9fba-4067-aedb-3619aea13b40"],
 " being an isolated equilibrium of X' = F[X].  If the eigenvalues of the \
corresponding linearized equations have negative real parts, then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {
       StyleBox[
        SubscriptBox["x1", "0"],
        FontWeight->"Bold"]},
      {
       StyleBox[
        SubscriptBox["x2", "0"],
        FontWeight->"Bold"]}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3f7a642a-fbf3-4b66-bf5d-0a1b2ff86802"],
 " is an attractor.  If either of the eigenvalues have a positive real part, \
then the equilibrium is unstable."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348059698*^9, 3.398348110977*^9}, 
   3.398351138738*^9},ExpressionUUID->"9810facb-ad42-4476-af7a-69a385160d6b"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The Phase Plane", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b3e6f762-422c-48d2-8cc2-1fe2f9e2299e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An autonomous second order equation can always the reduced to a first-order \
system.  \nFor example, if:\n\t\tx '' = f [ x, x ' ]\nthen the change a \
variable:\n\t\tx1 = x\n\t\tx2 = x '\nwill reduce the second-order ODE into a \
first-order system:\n\t\tx1'[t] = f1[x1,x2]\n\t\tx2'[t] = f2[x1,x2]\nIf, for \
example, x1 = x represents position, then x2 = x ' represents velocity.  \n\
Therefore, a plot of the vector field { f1[x1,x2], f2[x1,x2] }  vs. x1 and x2 \
represents a plot of the vector field vs. position and velocity.  Such a plot \
is called the \"phase plane\".\nTherefore, a plot of the \"phase plane\" \
often has an immediate physical interpretation.\n\n",
 StyleBox["Example",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": The nonlinear pendulum problem:\nRefer to Example 1.2 for the development \
of the second order ODE for the pendulum:\n\t\t\[Theta]''[t] = \
-r*\[Theta]'[t] - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox["g", "L"],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4fc94ca9-f08a-42a1-84ab-062408fb08f4"],
 "*Sin[\[Theta][t]]   where r =",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{" ", "k1"}], "m"],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "523acc57-c7eb-4e11-901c-ca8c0b993d75"],
 "\t\nReduce the second-order ODE into a first-order system:\n\t\tx1 = \
\[Theta]\t\t\t (angular position)\n\t\tx1' = \[Theta] ' = x2\t\t (angular \
velocity)\n\t\tx2' = \[Theta] '' =  -r*\[Theta] ' - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox["g", "L"],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "696e0f57-a5b2-4e4c-a6ea-c8bdb8fc7e6d"],
 "*Sin[\[Theta]] \n\t\t     =  -r*x2 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox["g", "L"],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "60124c07-0b6c-4980-910f-ad8677c0fa40"],
 "*Sin[x1] \nTherefore, a plot of { f1[x1,x2], f2[x1,x2] }  vs. x1 and x2 \
represents a plot of the vector field vs. angular position and angular \
velocity.  (For many problems, the position is related to the potential \
energy and the velocity is related to the kinetic energy.)\nGenerate a plot \
of the \"phase plane\" for the pendulum:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348123723*^9, 
  3.398348137334*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1e7f44c2-58c2-4fd8-9c12-200650c00dd4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x1_", ",", "x2_"}], "]"}], ":=", "x2"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1127]:=",ExpressionUUID->"61657e28-74bc-4979-bacc-ca36c188d22b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x1_", ",", "x2_"}], "]"}], ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", " ", "r"}], "*", "x2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["g", "L"], "*", 
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x1", "]"}]}]}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1128]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5805fd31-372c-407b-beae-9bbc83ef8cd2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"r", "=", ".8"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"L", "=", "1"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"g", "=", "9.8"}], ";"}]}], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348160646*^9, 3.398348171883*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1129]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ceb98f07-1bfd-44a9-88b8-f263e0b836dd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"VectorPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x1", ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x2", ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"VectorScale", "\[Rule]", ".04"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", "\[Rule]", "1"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Angular Position\>\"", ",", "\"\<Angular Velocity\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348189611*^9, 3.398348225016*^9}, {
   3.4639342591619177`*^9, 3.4639342748179674`*^9}, {3.463934340207755*^9, 
   3.4639343671449103`*^9}, 3.4639344242691793`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1132]:=",ExpressionUUID->"02b46a0c-0e0c-49b8-b04b-d4525d608d0e"],

Cell["\<\
The above plot has two interpretations:
 1: The vectors in the vector field will be parallel to a solution orbit.  \
Therefore, solutions displayed in the phase plane will follow both the \
direction and speed indicated by the vectors.
 2:  For this specific graph, the angular displacement is greatest when the \
angular velocity is the smallest, and correspondingly the angular velocity is \
greatest when the angular displacement is smallest.  This corresponds to the \
common observation that a pendulum's velocity reaches 0 at the extremes of \
its travel, and the pendulum's velocity is greatest when it is in the \
straight down position.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"163fbc86-ef48-47c1-80e1-49cb47200ac7"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Example 3.3
Nonlinear pendulum problem\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f867e67e-d1de-473b-bbdb-35cbaafcbeb1"],

Cell["\<\
A simple and historically important example of a nonlinear ODE is the \
pendulum problem.
The pendulum consist of a small bob of mass m attached to a slim, rigid \
massless rod of length l, which is connected to a pivot.  Thus, the motion of \
the mass will be restricted to a circular arc about the pivot as its center.  \
When the pendulum is displaced from a rest point the forces acting on the \
mass will be the force of gravity and a force of viscous damping.  For this \
discussion we will assume that the viscous damping will correspond to laminar \
flow which will generate a force opposite to the motion of the mass and \
proportional to the velocity (to the first power).
Because the rigid motion is restricted to be in a circular arc, then it is \
reasonable to express the position (arc length) as a function of a parameter \
(angle  \[Theta]).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398346162521*^9, {3.398348256775*^9, 3.398348268449*^9}, 
   3.398351417932*^9},ExpressionUUID->"7983892f-3ab3-4c1c-9fec-42b846dee9ec"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Animate", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"t3", "=", 
     RowBox[{".4", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", ".07"}], "t2"}]], 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "t2", "]"}]}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"Graphics3D", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Cylinder", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"5", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "t3", "]"}], ",", "0", ",", 
               RowBox[{"-", 
                RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "t3", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
          ".1"}], "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
        RowBox[{"Sphere", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"5", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "t3", "]"}], ",", "0", ",", 
             RowBox[{"-", 
              RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "t3", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], ",", ".5"}], 
         "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "2.5"}], ",", "2.5"}], "}"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "2"}], ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "6"}], ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"Boxed", "\[Rule]", "False"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}],
    ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t2", ",", "0", ",", 
     RowBox[{"6", " ", "2", "\[Pi]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"DefaultDuration", "\[Rule]", "10"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982819176454*^9, 3.3982820687444*^9}, {
   3.3982820999393997`*^9, 3.3982821864604*^9}, {3.3982822281324*^9, 
   3.3982823401344*^9}, {3.3982824400954*^9, 3.3982824558584003`*^9}, {
   3.3982824963864*^9, 3.3982825672743998`*^9}, 3.3982826207084*^9, {
   3.3982832614484*^9, 3.3982832752474003`*^9}, {3.398351504885*^9, 
   3.39835154617*^9}, {3.39835157902*^9, 3.3983516008900003`*^9}, {
   3.3983516377650003`*^9, 3.398351644642*^9}, {3.398351675573*^9, 
   3.3983517366*^9}, {3.398351771242*^9, 3.398351788476*^9}, {
   3.3986793649764547`*^9, 3.3986794076867294`*^9}, {3.398679519907881*^9, 
   3.398679524438812*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1133]:=",ExpressionUUID->"12b9df51-ae77-4d3a-b114-95e7775e7056"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nThe ODE is generated as a force balance on the mass:\n\n\t\ts[t] = L*\
\[Theta] [t]\n\t\ts'[t] = L*\[Theta] '[t]\n\t\ts''[t] = L*\[Theta] ''[t]\n\t\t\
m*a[t] = - k1*v[t]  - m*g*Sin[\[Theta][t]]\n\t\tm*L*\[Theta]''[t] = - k1*L*\
\[Theta]'[t] - m*g*Sin[\[Theta][t]]\n\t\t\[Theta]''[t] = -r*\[Theta]'[t] - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox["g", "L"],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "21df4306-a605-48cd-bb2a-0a0b00148f08"],
 "*Sin[\[Theta][t]]   where r =",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{" ", "k1"}], "m"],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4be95dee-2321-4d5e-894b-a20c780091bc"],
 "\t\nObserve that the above equation is nonlinear in the variable \[Theta].\n\
Let\n\t\tx1 = \[Theta]\n\t\tx1' = \[Theta] ' = x2\n\t\tx2' = \[Theta] '' =  \
-r*\[Theta] ' - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox["g", "L"],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4c550259-085c-4fdd-8f12-d15778cd0863"],
 "*Sin[\[Theta]] \n\t\t     =  -r*x2 - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox["g", "L"],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "247e06fc-ff38-4bfe-910b-e1d94221b550"],
 "*Sin[x1] "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398346162521*^9, {3.398348256775*^9, 3.398348268449*^9}, {
   3.398351417932*^9, 
   3.398351436024*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b07f5296-8616-4a0b-9707-464403eb50b7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "g", ",", "L", ",", "r", ",", "f1", ",", "f2", ",", "x1", ",", "x2"}], 
  "]"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1134]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2050371e-984e-43e1-b43d-21bf931e09d1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x1_", ",", "x2_"}], "]"}], ":=", "x2"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1135]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2a0bf476-5af2-4024-bd73-729a67780064"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x1_", ",", "x2_"}], "]"}], ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", " ", "r"}], "*", "x2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["g", "L"], "*", 
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x1", "]"}]}]}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1136]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b6ff75c2-fbdf-4a82-b9be-0942771791db"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"A", "=", 
  RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], " ", 
       RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], " ", 
       RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}]},
     {
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], " ", 
       RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], " ", 
       RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}]}
    }], ")"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398348303727*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1137]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9fecafec-74fd-4a2e-a8f0-d75e52d2a251"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"A", " ", "//", "MatrixForm"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1138]:=",ExpressionUUID->"bfc810da-e340-4754-bcde-dc3282dca31d"],

Cell["Evaluate the Jacobian matrix at the equilibrium point.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d4fc6e94-d487-4209-a422-35e4bd630921"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"A", " ", "/.", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x1", "\[Rule]", 
      SubscriptBox["x1", "0"]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"x2", "\[Rule]", 
      SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]}]}], "}"}]}], "//", "MatrixForm"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3983483172019997`*^9, 3.398348329943*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1139]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1871d691-836f-4bfe-b95b-24d7bb803d7a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["One",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " (of many) equilibrium states is at the origin."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398346174217*^9, {3.398352018175*^9, 
   3.398352036085*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"846172ac-45ee-48c6-bf6f-e4f8b31cd90f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["x1", "0"], "=", "0"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["x2", "0"], "=", "0"}], ";"}]}], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1140]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b0fce0fc-268e-4232-8cfd-be654bced579"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"A", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"A", " ", "/.", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x1", "\[Rule]", 
        SubscriptBox["x1", "0"]}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"x2", "\[Rule]", 
        SubscriptBox["x2", "0"]}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], 
  "\n"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"A", "//", "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348368524*^9, 3.398348381619*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1142]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1a61cdef-497c-4bdf-b8a5-4be42461965b"],

Cell["We can find the eigenvalues for the Jacobian matrix.", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398346176887*^9, 
  3.398346177207*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"04aeb5b4-7a7c-4881-a937-d0c7be83753d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["I", "M"], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", " ", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1144]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e6eb25c7-f713-4933-a7af-f6a97d721808"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Solve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
      RowBox[{"A", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "*", 
        SubscriptBox["I", "M"]}]}], " ", "]"}], "==", "0"}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[Lambda]"}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "TableForm"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39834839401*^9, 3.398348401961*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1145]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4c74d54f-e0ad-4772-8c3f-26b64ca313df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Thus, for the equilibrium point at the origin, the solution to the \
linearized ODE is always asymptotically stable if there is friction (i.e. r > \
0) (i.e. the real part of the eigenvalues \"-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "2"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "b0476d63-774c-4f02-aa19-d3e81b9adaa8"],
 " r\" will be negative when r > 0)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398346179124*^9, 3.3983461793710003`*^9}, {
  3.7493825522519455`*^9, 
  3.749382563272047*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cecc9bb1-64ed-42df-8f89-\
6d89573c32be"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Example 3.4
Electric Circuit\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6dde719f-7758-421e-909b-d96a2c2b1022"],

