/+ovp0vHSXu/07/b23uP/wu4hSEg\
\>"],ExpressionUUID->"8d02e454-330f-4456-a13b-fffa6e5425e5"]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7493833152142344`*^9, 3.7493833281565285`*^9}, {
  3.7493833623249445`*^9, 
  3.749383395301242*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"69e33e60-1ac9-4bf5-80e7-\
a5f1021d2ff0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A source of electrical energy supplies a voltage between two points in the \
circuit (voltage vC between a1 and a2).  This will cause current to flow.\n\
Next, consider what happens when the voltage source is suddenly removed.  \
What will happen to the current flow after that point in time?  A simple \
explanation is:\n\t  The stored electric charge (voltage) is drained from the \
capacitor.\n\t  The resulting current through the inductor increases \
generating a magnetic field.\n\t  Energy is ",
 StyleBox["gained",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " if the resistance of the resistor is negative (\[Alpha] > 0, physically \
unrealistic), or \n\t  energy is ",
 StyleBox["lost",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " if the resistance of the resistor is positive (\[Alpha] < 0, physically \
realistic).\n\t  The magnetic field in the inductor collapses inducing a \
reverse current through the resistor.\n\t  The reverse electric charge \
(voltage) on the capacitor increases.\n\t  The process cycles back and forth \
between these two states.\n\t  \nLet's do some standard bookkeeping on the \
voltage and current at various junctures in the circuit.  See the book for \
complete details. (Basically, this is a straightforward application of \
Kirchhoff's law for this specific circuit: also the voltage across the \
capacitor = the sum of the voltages across the resistor and inductor.)\nAn \
analysis of the circuit involves three voltages:\n \n\tvL = Voltage across \
the inductor\n \tvC = Voltage across the capacitor\n \tvR = Voltage across \
the resistor\n \nthus:   vC = vL + vR   \n \n\tu = total current across the \
circuit\n\t\nThe following relationships define the specific response of each \
electrical component:\n \n \tvL = u'\n\tvC = -",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "t"], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"u", "[", "s", "]"}], 
     RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "s"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "54552e56-c698-4ba6-80b7-541a05b3756f"],
 "\n \tvR = \[Alpha]*(",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "3"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c82c7d8d-a1f9-416e-83f0-2f91b6792c72"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["u", "3"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f3e638ba-2a1c-4f4b-9473-15d5d75c3df1"],
 " - u),    \[Alpha] > 0   This is a more accurate expression of Ohm's law.\n \
\tHowever, \[Alpha] > 0 corresponds to the physically impossible case of \
\"negative\" resistance.\n \t\nThis can be illustrated by examining a plot of \
Ohm's law as the current increases from 0 to 2:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398346183309*^9, 3.3983461916540003`*^9}, {
  3.749383353855098*^9, 
  3.7493833570524178`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"09802491-aaeb-4c95-b724-\
49d9b1a67dc3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", "\[Alpha]", "]"}], ";"}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "*", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        FormBox[
         FractionBox["1", "3"],
         TraditionalForm], 
        FormBox[
         SuperscriptBox["u", "3"],
         TraditionalForm]}], " ", "-", " ", "u"}], ")"}]}], " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"+", "1"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"u", ",", "0", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"Thickness", "[", ".01", "]"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1146]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1d3fc3a5-adc6-4975-ac63-efc76ff7ada5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Observe that the corresponding voltage response is negative for smaller \
values of the current.\n \nThe above equations can be converted into an \
integral-differential equation by substituting the current relationships to \
their corresponding voltages (vC = vL + vR), which yields:\n   \n\t -",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "t"], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"u", "[", "s", "]"}], 
     RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "s"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dccae020-62b5-46a2-af6b-c8fb6ff87cd1"],
 " =  u'[t] +  \[Alpha]*(",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "3"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "68c49c41-41b1-4dbe-a50d-750cfdec4689"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}], "3"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ef03d714-281e-4707-b731-ee6161ac949b"],
 " - u[t])\n \nDifferentiating this equation with respect to time yields a \
second order ODE, which is more convenient than a integral-differential \
equation.\n   "
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"35d0130d-4151-47a0-9a1d-9fbbfbcd1234"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], " ", 
  RowBox[{"(", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "t"], 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"u", "[", "s", "]"}], 
      RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "s"}]}]}], " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"u", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "*", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         FractionBox["1", "3"], " ", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}], "3"]}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", ")"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348443553*^9, 3.3983484486549997`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1148]:=",ExpressionUUID->"717bec38-d299-413c-8970-8958278a95f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This ODE is known as the Van der Pol equation.\n\nWe can express this \
equation as a first order system by defining:\n  \n  \tvC = vC\n  \tu = - vC' \
      (i.e. vC = -",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "t"], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"u", "[", "s", "]"}], 
     RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "s"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d7713127-89ab-4fba-b887-322eb5764ede"],
 ")\n  \n  \tvC' = vC' = - u\n  \tu'   = vL \n    \t      = vC - vR\n\t      \
= vC - \[Alpha]*(",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "3"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "31677d9e-2f82-4827-8717-7546cf1bbd99"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["u", "3"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b004d21e-1d22-4c42-a7a7-617f67318f9a"],
 " - u)\n  \nDefine the corresponding vector field for this system of \
nonlinear ODEs:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"81dc3404-d273-4019-997a-9b42f90b295f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
   RowBox[{"vC_", ",", "u_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "u"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"vC", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "*", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         FormBox[
          FractionBox["1", "3"],
          TraditionalForm], 
         FormBox[
          SuperscriptBox["u", "3"],
          TraditionalForm]}], " ", "-", " ", "u"}], ")"}]}]}]}], 
   "}"}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1149]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8b99f8c5-d83b-46d9-a875-4a362b0204f3"],

Cell["\<\
Find the equilibrium points for this field in terms of the voltage across the \
capacitor \"vC\" and current \"u\":\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"97beadab-fe31-4b4d-9b38-96895fe86912"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Solve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
      RowBox[{"vC", ",", "u"}], "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"vC", ",", "u"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], "  "}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348476909*^9, 3.398348483549*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1150]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a7bb8eb5-31af-48e2-95ce-c7aad2e4f3bd"],

Cell["\<\
Thus zero current and zero voltage represent the only rest point. 

Is this equilibrium point stable or unstable?
Look at the vector field to see the qualitative behavior of solutions to this \
system:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25915183-b876-486d-b354-8cefb9b6cd14"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "=", "1"}], ";"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1151]:=",ExpressionUUID->"bca4d386-651f-4225-a1a5-12d213e32cc1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"VectorPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
    RowBox[{"vC", ",", "u"}], "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"vC", ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", "7"}], ",", "7"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"u", ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", "7"}], ",", "7"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Capacitor Voltage\>\"", ",", "\"\<Current\>\""}], "}"}]}]}],
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348508344*^9, 3.398348571273*^9}, {
  3.4639345112055664`*^9, 3.4639345635486465`*^9}, {3.4639347639523315`*^9, 
  3.4639347917488503`*^9}, {3.4639348597792296`*^9, 3.4639348600136013`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1152]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1bb7d54d-640b-499b-93eb-b7d608683b4a"],

Cell["\<\
It is very hard to visualize the effect of the vector field because of the \
large variation in the lenght of the vectors.

Redraw the above vector field but rescale all vectors to have the same length:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.4639348731540585`*^9, 
  3.463934979433948*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d08e595b-1a31-4567-b13b-\
6540b6a4778c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"plot1A", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"VectorPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
     RowBox[{"vC", ",", "u"}], "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"vC", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "7"}], ",", "7"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"u", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "7"}], ",", "7"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"Frame", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"VectorScale", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{".04", ",", "Automatic", ",", "None"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"FrameLabel", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Capacitor Voltage\>\"", ",", "\"\<Current\>\""}], 
      "}"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348508344*^9, 3.398348571273*^9}, {
  3.4639345112055664`*^9, 3.4639345635486465`*^9}, {3.4639347639523315`*^9, 
  3.463934769139765*^9}, {3.463935801798422*^9, 3.4639358030952797`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1153]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e299d8f3-3519-41e9-b49d-e2eea9e0ac9b"],

Cell["Next, take a closer look at the equilibrium point:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398346205295*^9},ExpressionUUID->"41822d37-40cd-4626-bd3d-20fd6f96ec8d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"VectorPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
    RowBox[{"vC", ",", "u"}], "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"vC", ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"u", ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Capacitor Voltage\>\"", ",", "\"\<Current\>\""}], "}"}]}]}],
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348585973*^9, 3.398348611508*^9}, {
  3.4639350019180355`*^9, 3.463935031558281*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1154]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8e4119fc-4eaa-4416-a972-5d44c1322dbb"],

Cell["\<\
Redraw the above vector field but rescale all vectors to have the same length:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.4639348731540585`*^9, 3.463934979433948*^9}, {
  3.463935052964257*^9, 
  3.4639350535892487`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3fed9506-e6a0-48b4-a3c3-\
9bf02dbd6743"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"plot1B", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"VectorPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
     RowBox[{"vC", ",", "u"}], "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"vC", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"u", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"Frame", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"VectorScale", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{".04", ",", "Automatic", ",", "None"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"FrameLabel", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Capacitor Voltage\>\"", ",", "\"\<Current\>\""}], 
      "}"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348585973*^9, 3.398348611508*^9}, {
   3.4639350019180355`*^9, 3.4639350096210613`*^9}, 3.463935068401559*^9, {
   3.4639358443135023`*^9, 3.463935845297865*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1155]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0c22cc84-9936-4099-8cdc-6b68aef692df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It may be hard to tell from the above vector fields if the equilibrium \
point is stable or unstable.  We can either examine the behavior of specific \
solutions or calculate the eigenvalues for the Jacobian matrix.\n\nFirst, \
determine the behavior of the solutions (starting ",
 StyleBox["FAR",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " from the equilibrium point vC[0]=7, u[0]=7):"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.463935293633051*^9, 
  3.4639352941330447`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"71aefaa7-6a0d-4482-a10b-\
27b7a48fc7fb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"solutionRules", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["vC", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"vC", "[", "t", "]"}], "-", 
        RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           FractionBox[
            SuperscriptBox[
             RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}], "3"], "3"], "-", 
           RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"vC", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "7"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"u", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "7"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"vC", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "15"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398346469579*^9, 3.398346483867*^9}, {3.398348618199*^9,
   3.39834862434*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1156]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2be337f9-c2c8-45a8-8c39-92aa25449e09"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"vCNew", "[", "t_", "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"uNew", "[", "t_", "]"}]}], "}"}], "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"vC", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], "/.", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", "solutionRules", "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348635146*^9, 3.398348645074*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1157]:=",ExpressionUUID->"30725278-80b0-414a-9597-6255f11650cc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"plot2A", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"ParametricPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"vCNew", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"uNew", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "15"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"AxesLabel", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Voltage\>\"", ",", "\"\<Current\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"Red", ",", 
       RowBox[{"Thickness", "[", ".01", "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398348652434*^9, {3.463935190931241*^9, 3.4639351983061466`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1158]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4a5946fb-a45a-45d5-a6f7-bd60d7b462e1"],

Cell["Show both the vector field and the specific solution:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398346212701*^9},ExpressionUUID->"5fd466d3-4b2b-44b9-8320-eaf6591d1c0b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"Show", " ", "[", 
   RowBox[{"plot1A", ",", "plot2A"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"1d2de08b-cb42-4b77-986a-d2bb5b6e6447"],

Cell["\<\
The above graph suggests that solutions corresponding to initial conditions \
starting far from the equilibrium point will not converge towards the \
equilibrium point.

Next, take a closer look at the equilibrium point:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a12947d8-b285-40ce-9dde-e547c71dfb19"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"plot1B", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"VectorPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
     RowBox[{"vC", ",", "u"}], "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"vC", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"u", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "3"}], ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"Frame", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"VectorScale", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{".04", ",", "Automatic", ",", "None"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"FrameLabel", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Capacitor Voltage\>\"", ",", "\"\<Current\>\""}], 
      "}"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348672914*^9, 3.3983486983129997`*^9}, {
  3.4639351006511464`*^9, 3.4639351255883274`*^9}, {3.463935867860076*^9, 
  3.4639358690006866`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1159]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b4f49747-d3b2-455d-9093-1ad89df80457"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Next, consider a solution that starts ",
 StyleBox["extremely close",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " to the equilibrium point (vC[0]=.01, u[0]=0):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"742a89a1-f164-42bf-a980-a3f8e7500f0f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"solutionRules", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["vC", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"vC", "[", "t", "]"}], "-", 
        RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           FractionBox[
            SuperscriptBox[
             RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}], "3"], "3"], "-", 
           RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"vC", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", ".01"}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"u", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "0"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"vC", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "30"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39834649366*^9, 3.3983465066619997`*^9}, {
  3.398348704977*^9, 3.3983487094519997`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1160]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0e208516-6cb4-42b9-9ac1-d143b7d9ec00"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"vCNew", "[", "t_", "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"uNew", "[", "t_", "]"}]}], "}"}], "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"vC", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], "/.", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", "solutionRules", "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348717299*^9, 3.398348725226*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1161]:=",ExpressionUUID->"810c9416-1bcd-40d7-88ee-8b1ba4344dcf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"plot2B", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"ParametricPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"vCNew", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"uNew", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "30"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"AxesLabel", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Voltage\>\"", ",", "\"\<Current\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"Green", ",", 
       RowBox[{"Thickness", "[", ".01", "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.4639353588665915`*^9, 3.463935365444632*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1162]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4002ae14-5b36-4712-8763-45ba9faa40ff"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"Show", " ", "[", 
   RowBox[{"plot1B", ",", "plot2B"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1163]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ccca60bb-d764-41ce-a336-ad06a22d2864"],

Cell["\<\
The above graph suggests that solutions corresponding to initial conditions \
starting very close to the equilibrium point will be repelled from the \
equilibrium point and ultimately enter a stable orbit.
Therefore, it appears that are equilibrium point located at the origin is not \
an attractor (when \[Alpha] > 0).
It appears that the behavior of this system is to oscillate forever (which is \
inconsistent with the actual physical process, thereby invalidating this \
particular model (at least for the case where \[Alpha] > 0)).

Next, calculate the Jacobian for this system at the equilibrium point.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"02e9cd68-b1d0-40ba-8cf1-a490b8adee32"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", "f1"}], "]"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1164]:=",ExpressionUUID->"454ed114-62cb-4cc2-bf65-14bf6ff193e0"],

Cell["\<\
Enter the equations for the vector field for this ODE system:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"276babd8-d197-4681-b866-85a1658338fc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
   RowBox[{"vC_", ",", "u_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"-", "u"}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1165]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7a5d2a0f-fa4f-4d53-a009-ea441ddca422"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
   RowBox[{"vC_", ",", "u_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"vC", " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "*", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       FormBox[
        FractionBox["1", "3"],
        TraditionalForm], 
       FormBox[
        SuperscriptBox["u", "3"],
        TraditionalForm]}], " ", "-", " ", "u"}], ")"}]}]}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1166]:=",ExpressionUUID->"36707ef0-debf-4b40-b32e-7eaa8ae6c647"],

Cell["\<\
Next, calculate the Jacobian for this system (observe that the order of the \
first and second equations shown here are switched in the book):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7f252792-186e-4280-a421-360bfdc64d4e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"A", "=", 
    RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "vC"], " ", 
         RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
          RowBox[{"vC", ",", "u"}], "]"}]}], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "u"], " ", 
         RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
          RowBox[{"vC", ",", "u"}], "]"}]}]},
       {
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "vC"], " ", 
         RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
          RowBox[{"vC", ",", "u"}], "]"}]}], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "u"], " ", 
         RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
          RowBox[{"vC", ",", "u"}], "]"}]}]}
      }], ")"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"A", " ", "//", "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1167]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a52b6d38-0243-4d7d-8136-589e88745c70"],

Cell["\<\
Evaluate the Jacobian matrix at the equilibrium point (vC \[Rule] 0,u \[Rule] \
0).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cbc6b85e-f6b2-44cc-8bb9-2f316f69d4db"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"A", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"A", " ", "/.", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"vC", "\[Rule]", "0"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"u", "\[Rule]", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", "\t"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"A", " ", "//", "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348770156*^9, 3.398348778124*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1169]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1d308aba-1fe9-473c-914b-aee0401b3e4d"],

Cell["We can find the eigenvalues for the Jacobian matrix.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ca4c9531-6b62-4435-9ab6-ba63919e04e5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["I", "M"], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", " ", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1171]:=",ExpressionUUID->"12a3f62e-4068-4087-8c56-b58e3b05a4c4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Solve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
      RowBox[{"A", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "*", 
        SubscriptBox["I", "M"]}]}], " ", "]"}], "==", "0"}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[Lambda]"}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "TableForm"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348788359*^9, 3.3983487938190002`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1172]:=",ExpressionUUID->"70879d0e-36f2-4232-9c05-4248246dc012"],

Cell["\<\
Observe that if \[Alpha] > 0, then the real part of the eigenvalues are \
positive and the resulting system is unstable (which corresponds to our \
example where \[Alpha] = 1).  
However, if \[Alpha] < 0, then the real part of the eigenvalues are negative \
and the resulting system is locally asymptotically stable (which would be \
more consistent with the actual physical process).
Consider the case where \[Alpha] =  -1:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"753584b9-6fb2-40d8-8bb8-fc0ee205e94e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", "=", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], ";"}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1173]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ce96ab5a-2783-4d98-aa0d-25b8d1b9f538"],

Cell["\<\
First, determine the behavior of the solutions (starting far from the \
equilibrium point vC[0]=2, u[0]=0):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"296e9242-c367-4961-a415-88bf0ac57f48"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"solutionRules", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["vC", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"vC", "[", "t", "]"}], "-", 
        RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           FractionBox[
            SuperscriptBox[
             RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}], "3"], "3"], "-", 
           RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"vC", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "2"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"u", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "0"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"vC", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "15"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3983465153780003`*^9, 3.398346521006*^9}, {
  3.3983488040559998`*^9, 3.398348808083*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1174]:=",ExpressionUUID->"150195a3-ded0-430f-b7d0-f3d2f11aacf3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"vCNew", "[", "t_", "]"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"uNew", "[", "t_", "]"}]}], "}"}], "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"vC", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"u", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], "/.", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", "solutionRules", "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348817019*^9, 3.39834882455*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1175]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d22f9fc9-6e1e-4c53-80c3-af2ff8be3536"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"plot2C", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"ParametricPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"vCNew", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"uNew", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "15"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"PlotRange", "\[Rule]", "All"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"AxesLabel", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Voltage\>\"", ",", "\"\<Current\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"Red", ",", 
       RowBox[{"Thickness", "[", ".01", "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.4639354663808403`*^9, 3.463935471302652*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1176]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b64c6351-4b58-4f18-aff1-c60c309521d1"],

Cell["Next, plot the corresponding vector field:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"da555045-0ef1-4e91-8e23-a395887c7e20"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"plot1C", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"VectorPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "u"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"vC", "-", 
       RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          FractionBox[
           SuperscriptBox["u", "3"], "3"], "-", "u"}], ")"}]}]}]}], "}"}], 
    ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"vC", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "7"}], ",", "7"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"u", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "7"}], ",", "7"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"Frame", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"VectorScale", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{".04", ",", "Automatic", ",", "None"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"FrameLabel", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Capacitor Voltage\>\"", ",", "\"\<Current\>\""}], 
      "}"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348840064*^9, 3.3983488745810003`*^9}, {
  3.463935408334708*^9, 3.463935413069022*^9}, {3.4639354517872767`*^9, 
  3.4639354535528793`*^9}, {3.463935907156448*^9, 3.4639359086251793`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1177]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9ce0db67-eb04-46b2-9bdf-3b610778b07b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Observe that solutions corresponding to initial conditions with \
sufficiently large initial voltages and currents will produce unstable \
solutions (which of course is physically unrealistic).  However, for smaller \
values of the initial voltage and current, the solutions will be \
asymptotically stable (i.e. will converge to the equilibrium point \
corresponding to 0 voltage and 0 current, which is physically realistic -- \
look at the equation for resistance:  vR = \[Alpha]*(",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "3"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "59a4c5d4-5ea0-4b19-bd36-bde5bcc153b6"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["u", "3"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "72c14e22-464c-4e48-b72f-b2cd5c3b47ec"],
 " - u), which clearly indicates that \[Alpha] < 0 for smaller values of the \
current \"u\" correspond to a ",
 StyleBox["positive",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " resistance -- which is the only physically realistic case).\nShow both the \
vector field and this specific solution:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eeae2c4b-b56b-4068-acd4-26c3f6829723"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"Show", " ", "[", 
   RowBox[{"plot1C", ",", "plot2C"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1178]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a681b9d9-9e21-4f9f-aa03-a2bf5b1df41f"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Example 3.5
Eigenvalues: Re(\[Lambda]) =  0\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"45f61437-ed82-45f5-8f04-fc979bb09758"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The case of an ODE which is stable, but not asymptotically stable is more \
difficult.  If the linearized ODE is only stable and not asymptotically \
stable, then we can not predict the behavior of the nonlinear ODE system \
using the behavior of the corresponding linear system.  \nConsider the \
following example of a nonlinear ODE system:\n\t\t\tx1' =",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"     ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"x2", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", "*", "x1", "*", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["x1", "2"], " ", "+", " ", 
        SuperscriptBox["x2", "2"]}], ")"}]}]}],
    FontWeight->"Bold"]}]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d18d6fd5-b29c-4a22-84f4-d317a019f4b7"],
 "\n\t\t\tx2' =",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{" ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", " ", "x1"}], " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", "*", "x1", "*", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["x1", "2"], " ", "+", " ", 
        SuperscriptBox["x2", "2"]}], ")"}]}]}]}],
   FontWeight->"Bold"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "391f4e93-177a-41d1-a0ac-87d91fd533ef"],
 "\t"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348900225*^9, 3.398348902186*^9}, {3.398348937645*^9,
   3.3983489391730003`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8d2176b1-9bdd-41e6-84c2-\
b58111bd2918"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", "[", "\[Epsilon]", "]"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1179]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c9e92390-6b9b-454e-a417-23c1a2b0058d"],

Cell["Define the vector field for the ODE system:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"baa98b7e-d477-46d4-8f5c-d329db92c7c7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x1_", ",", "x2_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "     ", 
  RowBox[{"x2", " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", "*", "x1", "*", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["x1", "2"], " ", "+", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["x2", "2"]}], ")"}]}]}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1180]:=",ExpressionUUID->"31f7e9b4-dd90-4612-aa65-bb4fa228aa5f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x1_", ",", "x2_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", " ", "x1"}], " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", "*", "x1", "*", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["x1", "2"], " ", "+", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["x2", "2"]}], ")"}]}]}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1181]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b9b42f14-a865-4767-bae1-a651f6aa0561"],

Cell["Find the equilibrium points in this field:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0bbc1cbe-df63-4d69-9ce2-fee4ec0b5afe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"Solve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], "\[Equal]", "0"}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], "\[Equal]", "0"}]}], 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3983489562130003`*^9, 3.398348959394*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1182]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c830ccf5-291e-4e9c-be83-55a2474d2fe6"],

Cell["\<\
The only real valued equilibrium point is at the origin.

Find the Jacobian corresponding to the linearized ODE system (expanded about \
the equilibrium point at the origin):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e48df184-ccac-45a0-a093-ced9e992bc10"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"A", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], " ", 
         RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
          RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], " ", 
         RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
          RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}]},
       {
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x1"], " ", 
         RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
          RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x2"], " ", 
         RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
          RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}]}
      }], ")"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"A", "  ", "//", "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1183]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4cccf7df-c155-4894-97ec-36dd1c287c6d"],

Cell["Examine the Jacobian at the equilibrium point:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f7d1e52-afab-4490-b5b6-b568b24cb45d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"A", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"A", " ", "/.", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x2", "\[Rule]", "0"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"x1", "\[Rule]", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"A", "      ", "//", "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1185]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d2aa05ef-522f-4f56-bd80-241cebfd7030"],

Cell["\<\
Observe that this is just a special case of our mass-spring system.

Calculate the corresponding eigenvalues for the Jacobian matrix:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"34f15864-b96c-450f-97d2-371039cc38c5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["I", "M"], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", " ", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1187]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2c8df020-5fd6-487c-b0ce-5a0c03c4f86b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Solve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
      RowBox[{"A", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", "*", 
        SubscriptBox["I", "M"]}]}], " ", "]"}], "==", "0"}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[Lambda]"}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "TableForm"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398348983191*^9, 3.3983489910030003`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1188]:=",ExpressionUUID->"37ba890f-69e5-4bc4-a3bb-36b5560f58f0"],

Cell["\<\
The eigenvalues do not have either positive or negative real parts.  \
Therefore, we cannot conclude that the nonlinear ODE system will be unstable \
or stable.

Consider a small damping term:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8b70b7e4-709c-4147-a208-1b1f085288fb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", "=", ".01"}], ";"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1189]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f94d93d0-87fd-41e9-88da-e4ffae37b734"],

Cell["Find the solution that starts at (2, 2).", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a850309f-35ca-4d4b-807d-07daecdb1fcf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"solutionRules", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["x1", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["x2", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x1", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "2"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x2", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "2"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "100"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3983465367279997`*^9, 3.398346542057*^9}, {
  3.3983490026210003`*^9, 3.398349005876*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1190]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2c018c9b-e8e6-4480-a0ef-99022b153cd7"],

Cell["Double check the solution at the initial time:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398346263374*^9, 
  3.398346263637*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d4cb835d-fe7f-4f20-983b-2594bea8caee"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
   "solutionRules"}], "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"t", "\[Rule]", "0"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398349016441*^9, 3.398349016698*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1191]:=",ExpressionUUID->"352a0afd-079a-4fa7-aa4a-279d10165c52"],

Cell["\<\
Which corresponds to what we specified above. 

Graph the solution in the phase plane.  
Observe that the solution moves clockwise.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"303af1df-43d6-4231-9c39-4a535481cbf3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"graph1", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"ParametricPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], "/.", "\[InvisibleSpace]", 
      "solutionRules"}], "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "100"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"AxesLabel", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<x1\>\"", ",", "\"\<x2\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "\[Rule]", "Red"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.4639355313331337`*^9, 3.4639355389267864`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1192]:=",ExpressionUUID->"50d964e2-33d6-40c2-817a-9e8ca724490e"],

Cell["Examine the corresponding vector field:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398346269243*^9, 
  3.398346269455*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"88088cf5-b45b-4d8a-966e-8e87f7d34c52"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"graph2", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"VectorPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x1", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "2.5"}], ",", "2.5"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x2", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "2.5"}], ",", "2.5"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"Frame", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"Frame", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"FrameLabel", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<x1\>\"", ",", "\"\<x2\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398349038172*^9, 3.398349076833*^9}, {
  3.463935514286477*^9, 3.4639355178176813`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1193]:=",ExpressionUUID->"eca83c3c-f921-4e2d-9c98-09e774a049b8"],

Cell["Superimpose the solution on the vector field:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.398346272814*^9},ExpressionUUID->"ec518e12-d0db-4f8a-8462-dcff0f4135e5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", 
  RowBox[{"graph2", ",", "graph1"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1194]:=",ExpressionUUID->"85e8365e-83cc-48c7-b293-c538009fcce4"],

Cell["\<\
 
Next, consider the case (somewhat impossible) of a negative damping (i.e. \
energy being added to be system).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d160cf85-775b-434e-9279-435c75fc89a2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Epsilon]", "=", 
   RowBox[{"-", ".01"}]}], ";"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1195]:=",ExpressionUUID->"55c85579-79e5-4bab-921b-1de096d7236b"],

Cell["  Find the solution:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c1d33963-ed41-4013-be18-d0e24092e5d6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"solutionRules", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["x1", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["x2", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x1", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "2"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x2", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "2"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "20"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3983465492530003`*^9, 3.3983465537130003`*^9}, {
  3.398349099451*^9, 3.3983491032869997`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1196]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3fc14366-388d-45ca-8f26-3b25b700c399"],

Cell[TextData[{
 " What is the problem here?  (Note that the solution moves clockwise then \
therefore cycles ",
 StyleBox["away",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " from the equilibrium point)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ec1814ad-f7d8-490e-bf76-c123c884b89f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"graph3", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"ParametricPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], "/.", "\[InvisibleSpace]", 
      "solutionRules"}], "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "11.53"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]",
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"PlotRange", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "10"}], ",", "10"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"Red", ",", 
       RowBox[{"Thickness", "[", ".01", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"AxesLabel", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<x1\>\"", ",", "\"\<x2\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.463935572020113*^9, 3.463935580004386*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1197]:=",ExpressionUUID->"935b8c8c-b95e-4acd-b2a9-1a3046e8699f"],

Cell["\<\
  Check the value of the solution at the time corresponding to where the \
above solution of the ODE fails:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"03bade27-9422-4eb8-a4b0-369e31c8eb1d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
   "solutionRules"}], "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"t", "\[Rule]", "11.53"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3983491244309998`*^9, 3.398349125527*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1198]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ede7aeee-71f2-4997-8143-79e614cfcda9"],

Cell["\<\
This indicates that the solution is moving away with tremendous speed,
Look at the corresponding vector field (when the solution is ok).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bbc010c5-647d-46ad-ab94-5a975b5a41d4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"VectorPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x1", ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", "10"}], ",", "10"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x2", ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", "10"}], ",", "10"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<x1\>\"", ",", "\"\<x2\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3983491363710003`*^9, 3.398349169367*^9}, {
  3.4639355887542734`*^9, 3.463935592629224*^9}, {3.46393574918972*^9, 
  3.463935768455098*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1199]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d9bd3d78-6a30-4c83-a6bf-e740e804468a"],

Cell["\<\
It is very hard to visualize the effect of the vector field because of the \
large variation in the lenght of the vectors.

Redraw the above vector field but rescale all vectors to have the same length:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.4639348731540585`*^9, 
  3.463934979433948*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3a3c2538-93fa-4e8a-9015-\
dc0b2c200216"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"graph4", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"VectorPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x1", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "10"}], ",", "10"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x2", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "10"}], ",", "10"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"Frame", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"VectorScale", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{".03", ",", "Automatic", ",", "None"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"FrameLabel", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<x1\>\"", ",", "\"\<x2\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3983491363710003`*^9, 3.398349169367*^9}, {
   3.4639355887542734`*^9, 3.463935592629224*^9}, 3.46393574918972*^9, {
   3.46393600113962*^9, 3.463936010764497*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1200]:=",ExpressionUUID->"282d0842-44c1-40dd-b7b3-a973ad2b7a01"],

Cell["  Examine the vector field over a greater range:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b1a7e76-aff5-4fd5-b527-c1b86f12677b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"graph5", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"VectorPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"f2", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x1", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "50"}], ",", "50"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x2", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "50"}], ",", "50"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"Frame", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"VectorScale", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{".03", ",", "Automatic", ",", "None"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"FrameLabel", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<x1\>\"", ",", "\"\<x2\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398349178041*^9, 3.398349220526*^9}, {
  3.463935601847856*^9, 3.463935607316536*^9}, {3.4639356630345726`*^9, 
  3.463935721393201*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1201]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f56adf4d-780c-4056-90e4-694dd68feba2"],

Cell["\<\
Display the solution and first vector field together:
Observe that the solution moves clockwise away from the equilibrium point.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c3f333c5-4d7b-49a7-afd0-16d1e2bd2787"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", 
  RowBox[{"graph3", ",", "graph4"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1202]:=",ExpressionUUID->"90f545b2-bd6e-47b0-bc07-70f50fc8fd29"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This example illustrates that the stability of a stable linearized system \
(which is not asymptotically stable) can not be used to predict the stability \
of the nonlinear system.  It is also distressing that a very small \
perturbation of the original stable system can produce vastly different \
results (both asymptotically stable and unstable).  \nThis has ",
 StyleBox["major",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " implications for modeling, where it is understood that any equation that \
describes a physical system is only approximate at best.  Thus, unless the \
resulting model is strongly asymptotically stable, then it is expected that \
small discrepancies in the equation coefficients will produce highly \
unpredictable results (eliminating the utility of the model)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e3cd394f-fc2c-47b4-b41c-76d8db929ed7"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Discrete Versus Continuous Models",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7904a4b5-835d-43ca-8aa5-\
82098d862a24"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Introduction", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"29c5df3f-1081-468f-ab12-96ffff8fc92f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 " For many problems, it is more convenient to conceive of the problem as a \
discrete problem rather than a continuous problem.  For example, the \
population growth of buffalo might be better modeled as occurring once a year \
at a specific time, rather than on a continuous basis.\nThe primarily \
difference in the definition of our models is the use of discrete rather than \
continuous functions, and the use of difference rather than differential \
equations.\n\nSuppose that our population is defined (i.e. measured) only at \
discrete times:  i*\[CapitalDelta]t\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"n", "[", "i_", "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"n", "[", 
     RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"7a8b6e8e-1521-4ef5-b675-8ad21435d149"],
 "\n\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n", "'"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], " ", "\[TildeTilde]"}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"fff401bc-ec4d-42f7-a6ca-c81c405865e4"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{" ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"n", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"i", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}],
         "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"n", "[", 
        RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}]}]}], "\[CapitalDelta]t"],
    FontSize->16,
    FontWeight->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ba62408c-e185-4a94-a0d6-a4c1ac672102"],
 "    (Approximately)\n\n\t \t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"n", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"i", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], 
     "]"}], " ", "\[TildeTilde]", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n", "[", 
      RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"n", "'"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], " ", "*", " ", 
      "\[CapitalDelta]t", " "}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5990b228-c0f3-4584-83d3-2bcb5f01193f"],
 "     (Approximately) \n if:  \n\t \t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"n", "'"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"f", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", "[", 
       RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " "}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"b64a2e62-fe0f-42eb-b376-78b3e136f195"],
 "\n then: \n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"n", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"i", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], 
     "]"}], " ", "\[TildeTilde]", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n", "[", 
      RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"f", "[", 
       RowBox[{"n", "[", 
        RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "*", " ", 
      "\[CapitalDelta]t", " "}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e33a19c6-94e7-4a4d-bfc9-2b49bda96166"],
 "    (Approximately)"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398349242725*^9, 3.398349248507*^9}, {3.398349426582*^9,
   3.3983494540550003`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8f29608f-709c-4781-b404-\
f32c2fe31502"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Population growth (discrete model)", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"1f677c51-46fc-458d-a9fa-8db55d3388f5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Suppose that our population is defined (i.e. measured) only at discrete \
times: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3961d0a8-30d9-40bd-855e-fa43aefe6579"],
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\t\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"n", "[", "i_", "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"n", "[", 
       RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}]}], "\n", "\n", "\t\t", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"n", "'"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], " ", "\[TildeTilde]", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"n", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"i", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}],
         "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"n", "[", 
          RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], "/", 
         "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "    ", 
        RowBox[{"(", "Approximately", ")"}]}]}]}], "\n", "\n", "\t \t", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"n", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"i", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], 
       "]"}], " ", "\[TildeTilde]", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"n", "[", 
        RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"n", "'"}], "[", 
         RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], " ", "*", " ", 
        "\[CapitalDelta]t", "      ", 
        RowBox[{"(", "Approximately", ")"}], " "}]}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"b0682a98-09cd-4c50-aa19-7086a80e755c"],
 "\n if:  \n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\t \t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"n", "'"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"f", "[", 
        RowBox[{"n", "[", 
         RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"then", ":", "\n", " ", "\n", "\t \t", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"n", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"i", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "*", 
          "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], " ", "\[TildeTilde]", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"n", "[", 
          RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"f", "[", 
           RowBox[{"n", "[", 
            RowBox[{"i", "*", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "*", 
          " ", "\[CapitalDelta]t", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"(", "Approximately", ")"}]}]}]}]}]}], "\n", "\t \t", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"n", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "=", " ", "initialPop"}]}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"b5562345-7d37-42c5-a2af-3c9a196c45c4"],
 "\n \nThe above formula can be implemented using several of the programming \
techniques that we have covered previously.\n  ",
 StyleBox["Use recursion",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 ":\n  (Warning!  Do not use recursion on large finite difference \
calculations, because recursion (unless more carefully defined) re-calculates \
all of the intermediate steps for each and every time step.)"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398349253066*^9, 3.3983492781400003`*^9}, {
  3.3983493848129997`*^9, 
  3.398349406322*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1b70d173-1bc9-455a-8e19-e400ecfb61b8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "r1", " ", ",", "k", ",", " ", "\[CapitalDelta]t", ",", "initialPop", ",", 
   "nPop", ",", "growthRate"}], "]"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1203]:=",ExpressionUUID->"86e69bb5-96f6-4720-a8e9-5f2311fb18f6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nPop", "[", "0", "]"}], ":=", " ", "initialPop"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1204]:=",ExpressionUUID->"25aa1222-b27d-4450-b18d-aa1ba951ed2f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nPop", "[", "n_", "]"}], ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"nPop", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}], "]"}], " ", "+", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"growthRate", "[", 
     RowBox[{"nPop", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "*", " ", 
    "\[CapitalDelta]t"}]}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1205]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a7885248-6eac-4801-bba3-3f23bc9a8ed1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"?", "nPop"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1206]:=",ExpressionUUID->"47c8d318-4d90-444e-b938-7aa2fd58fcfc"],

Cell[" Consider the first few values:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b6714354-1370-485d-ae5f-b0e7caaa9453"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nPop", "[", "0", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1207]:=",ExpressionUUID->"07324c8c-bbbc-40b2-ab3a-646c3aa27fa5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nPop", "[", "1", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1208]:=",ExpressionUUID->"357ec78a-cdee-412c-80b2-ee9436a217a2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nPop", "[", "2", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1209]:=",ExpressionUUID->"dffaff62-6712-4131-a683-23492273595a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"nPop", "[", "3", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1210]:=",ExpressionUUID->"6f5409cb-a4cd-43f7-b39c-0297529023b7"],

Cell["\<\
Define a function that represents the specific \"growthRate\" function \
corresponding to your model (for our example, use the Logistic growth model), \
and assign some values for the time step \[CapitalDelta]t and initial \
conditions:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fc50fbaf-ad15-4d5d-87a1-70b207817f61"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"growthRate", "[", "n_", "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"r1", "*", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
     FractionBox["n", "k"]}], ")"}], "*", "n"}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1211]:=",ExpressionUUID->"50967c13-d17c-41f1-ae39-4b806c42ed98"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"r1", "=", " ", ".1"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"k", "=", "1000"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]t", "=", "5"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"initialPop", "=", " ", "210"}], ";"}]}], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.398349319311*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1212]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d77c4a36-dc07-46d3-a832-2d40c11c8d30"],

Cell["\<\
 Generate a list of time-population points using the Table command:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15ef91e3-fc3e-456c-86ff-fbd857e8863b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"data1", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"i", " ", "\[CapitalDelta]t"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"nPop", "[", "i", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"i", ",", "0", ",", "10"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", "data1", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.398349326829*^9, 3.398349342873*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1216]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ec00d5d4-ff46-4b52-9bdd-7e5ce3414bfb"],

Cell[" Plot this list of data:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1a3edca5-bd60-4e36-94a1-12da9c2aa9ac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListPlot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"data1", ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "51"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", "1000"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"PointSize", "[", "0.02", "]"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7493841438470893`*^9, 3.7493841476854725`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1219]:=",ExpressionUUID->"29bdc38e-1fc4-4e31-8093-12d231f1f035"],

Cell["\<\
 This solution is similar to the one we found earlier for the logistic \
equation.  It is also possible to study the stability of discrete systems \
using techniques similar to those used to study continuous systems, however \
this is not the purpose of this course.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"02116d71-f280-4187-a3be-0ad9647baa8f"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]]
}, Open  ]]
},
